cleanFindings.suggestedFix:
Wrap subprocess.run in try/except CalledProcessError and print a user-friendly error message to stderr, then exit with non-zero code. Example:

try:
    subprocess.run(["cat", str(safe_path)], check=True)
except subprocess.CalledProcessError as e:
    print(f"Error reading log file: {e}", file=sys.stderr)
    sys.exit(1)
